# BUGS

The following are the bugs I am aware of; matter of fact, they're
bugs affecting the running environment, rather than SDL_bgi itself.

- Automatic refresh does not work on NVIDIA GK208BM (GeForce 920M) with 
nvidia-driver-* on GNU/Linux. As far as I can say, this is an NVIDIA
driver problem.

- On MSYS2, keyboard-related functions may cause the program to freeze
and/or hang. I've tried hard to find out, but I give up: I assume that
it's a bug in MSYS2 and/or associated libraries/software.

- The Python port is much less responsive to mouse clicks and key
presses than the C version.

Please report bugs if you find any.
